00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/insider/story/_/id/41668153/fantasy-football-streaming-last-minute-pickups-2024-week-6","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football free agent pickups: Look to New York for WR replacements","description":"Eric Moody highlights the players fantasy managers should consider adding off the waiver wire for Week 5, including WR replacements for Rashee Rice.","published":"2024-09-30T19:48:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFWaiverWirePickUp-41134236/nfl-fantasy-football-free-agent-pickups-waiver-wire-2024-week-5","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Moody","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football last-minute pickups: Justin Fields and emerging running backs, tight ends","description":"If injuries or disappointing performances have prompted you to find replacements, Matt Bowen has you covered, highlighting options with favorable setups this week.","published":"2024-09-27T13:44:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/insider/story/_/id/41399638/fantasy-football-streaming-last-minute-pickups-2024-week-4","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football free agent pickups Week 4: Covering for injured quarterbacks","description":"Need a fill-in for an injured QB like Justin Herbert, Tua Tagovailoa or Jordan Love? Eric Moody provides his waiver wire suggestions for Week 4.","published":"2024-09-23T20:27:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFWaiverWirePickUp-41134235/nfl-fantasy-football-free-agent-pickups-waiver-wire-2024-week-4","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Moody","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LaFleur's response to Packers center vomiting on ball tops Week 2 quotes","description":"Matt LaFleur held court about a bizarre sequence involving center Josh Myers vomiting on the ball pre-snap after the Packers' win.","published":"2024-09-16T13:38:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/41277510/nfl-week-2-best-quotes-matt-lafleur-packers-justin-fields-steelers-russell-wilson","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Jets coach Robert Saleh looking to 'reconnect' the dots","description":"After three straight losing seasons, New York's coach is taking a different approach heading into season.","published":"2024-09-02T14:06:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/41057500/new-york-jets-coach-robert-saleh-reaches-pivotal-year-4","type":"Story","byline":"Rich Cimini","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Adam Schefter's fantasy football cheat sheet: Value picks and sleepers to target","description":"No one is more plugged in to the latest buzz around the NFL than Adam Schefter. We asked him to share his favorite values in fantasy drafts with you.","published":"2024-08-24T14:29:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/insider/story/_/id/40887090/2024-fantasy-football-sleepers-cheat-sheet-adam-schefter","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Schefter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aaron Rodgers demonstrates short fuse, leadership in camp","description":"New York hasn't had this kind of leader at quarterback in a long time.","published":"2024-08-04T17:25:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/40711332/new-york-jets-aaron-rodgers-notebook-training-camp","type":"Story","byline":"Rich Cimini","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tyler Conklin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Conklin","description":"American football player (born 1995)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:49:38Z","intro":"Tyler Conklin (born July 30, 1995) is an American professional football tight end for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played one season of college basketball at Northwood before transferring to Central Michigan to play college football. He was selected by the Minnesota Vikings in the fifth round of the 2018 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Conklin attended L'Anse Creuse High School - North in Macomb Township, Michigan, where he was a standout two-sport athlete, playing as a wide receiver in football and combo guard in basketball. As a junior, Conklin led his basketball team to the Class A Final Four, scoring 22 points in a 59–46 semifinal loss to eventual state champion Saginaw High."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"After graduating from high school, Conklin was awarded a full-ride basketball scholarship to Division II Northwood University. He stayed for one semester and played in seven games, averaging 2.6 rebounds, 1.9 points and 1.4 assists per game. However, after the conclusion of the fall 2013 semester, Conklin realized he was unhappy and wanted to pursue a career in football. He transferred to Central Michigan University, where he walked on to the football team in the spring of 2014. The Central Michigan coaching staff initially wanted him to play defensive end, despite Conklin's strong desire to play tight end. He began the process of transferring again, this time to play tight end with his close friend and former high school quarterback at NAIA Siena Heights University. However, when the Central Michigan coaching staff learned of this, they convinced him to stay, agreeing to let him play tight end and assuring him that he'd have the opportunity to earn a scholarship in the spring of 2015.\nComing in at only 195 pounds, Conklin redshirted for his first season with the Chippewas, playing on the scout team while adding weight. After gaining 25 pounds during the offseason, he earned a scholarship and a role as a backup tight end for the 2015 season, playing in all 13 games and catching six passes for 95 yards. …"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"Conklin performed well at the 2018 NFL Combine and ranked second among all tight ends in the vertical, fourth in the broad jump, fifth in the three-cone drill, and ninth in the 40-yard dash.\n\nMINNESOTA VIKINGS\nConklin was selected by the Minnesota Vikings in the fifth round (157th overall) of the 2018 NFL draft. On May 5, 2018, Conklin signed a four-year contract worth $2.741 million, including a signing bonus of $281,032. In the Vikings' season opener against the San Francisco 49ers, he had one reception for six yards in his NFL debut.\nIn Week 15 of the 2020 season against the Chicago Bears, Conklin recorded 3 catches for 57 yards and his first career receiving touchdown during the 33–27 loss.\n\nNEW YORK JETS\nOn March 18, 2022, Conklin signed a three-year, $21 million contract with the New York Jets. He played in all 17 games (starting 16) for New York, recording 58 receptions for 552 yards and three touchdowns.\nConklin again appeared in all 17 games for the Jets during the 2023 campaign, compiling 62 receptions for 621 scoreless yards. He made 16 appearances (including 15 starts) for New York in 2024, recording 51 receptions for 449 yards and a career-high four touchdowns.\n\nLOS ANGELES CHARGERS\nOn March 21, 2025, Conklin signed a one-year, $3 million contract with the Los Angeles Chargers. He made 13 appearances (five starts) for Los Angeles, splitting time with Oronde Gadsden II, and logged seven receptions for 101 yards.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn March 13, 2026, Conklin signed with the Detroit Lions on a one-year contract. On August 30, he was released by the Lions as a part of final roster cuts. On September 1, Detroit re–signed Conklin to their 53–man roster."}],"wikidataId":"Q52423823","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-08-05","text":"Reinstated TE Tyler Conklin from the active/PUP list. Signed WR Tarik Black. Placed TE Miles Kitselman on injured reserve. Reverted WR Lawrence Keys to injured reserve after he cleared waivers."},{"date":"2026-07-26","text":"Placed DBs Brian Branch, Kerby Joseph and TE Tyler Conklin on the active/PUP list."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3915486","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/C/ConkTy00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tyler-conklin/47124","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tyler-conklin/7042","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Conklin"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.1M is the 41st-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Drafted 157th overall in 2018 (round 5) by MIN."]}